# IIQ Angular 18 File Placement

Located in `web/ui/ts/`. This is the **Angular 18** codebase — separate from legacy AngularJS in `web/ui/js/`.

```
web/ui/ts/
├── common/                 Shared across features
│   ├── components/         Reusable UI components (forms, tables, dropdowns)
│   ├── services/           Shared business logic services
│   ├── core/               Core modules (translation, timeout, config)
│   ├── pipes/              Custom Angular pipes
│   └── directives/         Custom directives
├── <feature-name>/         Feature modules (applicationDefinition, certification, etc.)
│   ├── components/         Feature-specific components
│   │   └── template/       HTML templates (imported via !text plugin)
│   ├── services/           Feature business logic
│   ├── store/              NgRx state (actions, reducers, effects, selectors) — where used
│   └── interfaces/         TypeScript interfaces (.interface.ts)
└── index.d.ts              Global type definitions
```

| File type | Location | Example |
|-----------|----------|---------|
| **Shared component** | `web/ui/ts/common/components/{name}/` | `web/ui/ts/common/components/dropdown/dropdown.component.ts` |
| **Shared service** | `web/ui/ts/common/services/` | `translation.service.ts` |
| **Feature component** | `web/ui/ts/{feature}/components/{name}/` | `web/ui/ts/applicationDefinition/components/reconfigure-modal/reconfigure-modal.component.ts` |
| **Feature service** | `web/ui/ts/{feature}/services/` | `application-definition.service.ts` |
| **Component template** | Inside `template/` subfolder of component | `dropdown/template/dropdown.component.html` |
| **NgRx files** | `web/ui/ts/{feature}/store/` | `application-definition.actions.ts`, `.reducer.ts`, `.effects.ts` |
| **Interfaces** | `web/ui/ts/{feature}/interfaces/` | `application-data.interface.ts` |
| **Module file** | `web/ui/ts/{feature}/{feature}.module.ts` | Register all components, services, imports here |

**Reference module:** Study `web/ui/ts/applicationDefinition/` as a complete example.

**Decision: Angular 18 or AngularJS?**
- New feature being built → `web/ui/ts/` (Angular 18)
- Modifying existing feature → match what's already there (don't mix frameworks within a feature)
